# Tracer: LogQuotient on every checked positive nonunit real base.
#
# Before (same code rejected by current equality search; legacy accepted):
# forall a,x,y R+:
#     a<1
#     =>:
#         log(a,x/y)=log(a,x)-log(a,y)
# Former behavior: log WD passed, equality BR still required 1<a.
#
# Now: the original exact statement verifies under its original domain.
forall a,x,y R+:
    a<1
    =>:
        log(a,x/y)=log(a,x)-log(a,y)

forall a,x,y R+:
    a!=1
    =>:
        log(a,x/y)=log(a,x)-log(a,y)

forall a,x,y R+:
    1<a
    =>:
        log(a,x/y)=log(a,x)-log(a,y)

# Boundary: nonpositive/unit bases, nonpositive arguments and wrong identities
# still reject; power WD and inherited premise permissions are retained.
# Executable negative boundaries: tests/unit/execute/log_algebra_base/tests.rs
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/log_quotient_valid_base.lit
# Owner: by_equality_identities_wave2.rs and log_algebra_base_proof.rs
